{
  "id": "29433_kakitsuzukeru",
  "headword": "{書|か}き{続|つづ}ける",
  "reading": "かきつづける",
  "romaji": "kakitsuzukeru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to keep writing; to continue writing",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to keep writing; to continue writing",
      "explanation": "To continue the act of writing without stopping. A compound of {書|か}く (to write) and {続|つづ}ける (to continue)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29433_kakitsuzukeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{手紙|てがみ}を{書|か}き{続|つづ}ける。",
      "english": "to keep writing a letter.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29433_kakitsuzukeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{朝|あさ}まで{小説|しょうせつ}を{書|か}き{続|つづ}けた。",
      "english": "He kept writing his novel until morning.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29433_kakitsuzukeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "どんなに{忙|いそが}しくても、{彼女|かのじょ}は{毎日|まいにち}{日記|にっき}を{書|か}き{続|つづ}けている。",
      "english": "No matter how busy she is, she keeps writing in her diary every day.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound verb: {書|か}く (to write) + {続|つづ}ける (to continue). Conjugates as an ichidan verb on the {続|つづ}ける ending.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Transitive; the thing written takes を: {手紙|てがみ}を{書|か}き{続|つづ}ける.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {小説|しょうせつ}を{書|か}き{続|つづ}ける: to keep writing a novel\n- {何|なに}があっても{書|か}き{続|つづ}ける: to keep writing no matter what\n\nUSAGE:\n- The pattern verb stem + {続|つづ}ける attaches to many verbs to mean \"keep doing,\" e.g. {走|はし}り{続|つづ}ける (keep running), {言|い}い{続|つづ}ける (keep saying).",
